          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కాపాడు (kāpāḍu) is native Dravidian. DEDR 1416 lists kāpāḍu, \"to protect, save\", under kācu, \"to guard\", with Tamil kā, \"to guard\". DEDR compares Prakrit kāhila, \"cowherd\"."
